5. P4 — ИСТОРИЯ, ПАМЯТЬ И TASK CONTINUITY
======================================================================

The latest 100 user-facing messages may be the default UI viewport.
They are not the retention limit.

All original messages, tool events and result records remain durably stored
according to the documented retention contract.

Do not replace raw messages with summaries.
Do not claim that every historical message is in the active model window.

Use deterministic retrieval:
- exact message/turn/event lookup;
- SQLite FTS5/BM25;
- exact paths, identifiers, code symbols, version and commit indexes;
- task/action links with provenance.

No embeddings or vector database are required.
No additional LLM call is required merely to rewrite every search query.

The user must be able to:
- open exact message 34;
- ask what was said in message 34;
- inspect the actual source event;
- ask what remains unfinished from recommendations in message 107;
- see specific action items and their actual status;
- jump to the original recommendation, related code changes and test evidence.

A task is not done because the model said "done". Done requires linked
execution/verification evidence.

Derived indexes must be rebuildable from canonical history.
Index failure must not destroy raw records.
Cross-session/project retrieval leaks are P0 failures.

Test:
- 100,000-event synthetic session;
- exact early-message retrieval;
- retrieval among distractors;
- corrections and supersession;
- cross-session isolation;
- tool-output lookup;
- corrupt index rebuild;
- export/import integrity;
- context budget overflow without destroying history;
- restart/reopen;
- false or unsupported retrieval.

Report actual storage size, reopen time, lookup latency and retrieval metrics.
Do not fabricate performance values.

